response:
**Gates before launch.** First I confirm that `spe/predictions/r04.yaml` and `spe/plans/r04.md` sit in the `SPE r04 predict` commit and have no edits since then. Next I run the grader selftest. `grade.py` must score the oracle labels from `answers.json` at 100%, and it must score empty labels and deliberately wrong labels at 0%. I check the judge the same way. `judge.md` must score a few known-good replies above a few known-bad ones. Then I regrade the r03 results with the r04 grader and judge to make a control. If the r03 numbers move, the grader changed, and I log that before any trial runs. I also confirm that the runner gives config B 6 tools and gives C2 3 tools plus `check_status`. Last, I dry-run the script on 3 cells with `{"only":["B:T001","C2:T001","C2:T017"],"spendCapUsd":2}`. The dry run passes when every trial matches its schema, the grader and judge return a result for every trial, the leak scan is clean, and each trial reports a real cost. I use that measured cost to check whether $40 covers 500 main trials plus top-ups. When all of this passes, I commit `SPE r04 evaluate (harness): ...` and launch.

I did not read `r03-workflow.js`, because this trial allowed no tools. The comments at the top of the script name 3 guesses to check against r03 before the dry run. They are the runner command, the tickets file path, and the command-line flags for `grade.py`.

```js
export const meta = {
  name: 'spe-r04-ticket-triage',
  description: 'SPE round 4. Configs B and C2 on 50 tickets, 5 trials per cell. Code grader for label.category and label.priority, Opus judge for reply tone, $40 spend cap.',
  phases: ['Setup', 'Trials', 'Grade', 'Judge', 'Top-up', 'Synthesis'],
};

// Copied in shape from spe/evals/harness/r03-workflow.js. Check these against r03 before the dry run:
// 1. A.runner is the command r03 used to run one config on one ticket. It prints one JSON object
//    with label, reply, tool_calls, tool_call_log, tool_errors, input_tokens, output_tokens, runtime_ms, cost_usd.
// 2. A.ticketsPath lists the tickets with an id field.
// 3. grade.py takes --answers and --input and prints one JSON line per trial.
// All cost estimates below are unmeasured until the dry run.

const ROUND = 'r04';

const DEFAULTS = {
  configs: ['B', 'C2'],
  trialsPerCell: 5,
  topUpMax: 5,               // extra trials per cell where only some trials passed
  spendCapUsd: 40,
  synthReserveUsd: 2,        // held back so the report still runs if trials hit the cap
  est: { setupUsd: 0.05, trialAgentUsd: 0.02, runnerUsd: 0.03, gradeUsd: 0.04, judgeUsd: 0.10, synthUsd: 0.50 },
  only: null,                // dry run, e.g. ['B:T001', 'C2:T017']
  expectTickets: 50,
  ticketsPath: 'spe/evals/tasks/tickets.json',
  runner: 'python spe/evals/harness/run_trial.py',
  model: 'opus',
};
const A = { ...DEFAULTS, ...(args || {}), est: { ...DEFAULTS.est, ...((args && args.est) || {}) } };

const OUT = `spe/evals/results/${ROUND}`;
const GRADER = 'spe/evals/graders/grade.py';
const ANSWERS = 'spe/evals/tasks/answers.json';
const JUDGE_RUBRIC = 'spe/evals/graders/judge.md';
const FORBIDDEN = /spe\/(evals|predictions|plans|prediction-log)/;

// ---------- helpers ----------
const range = n => Array.from({ length: n }, (_, i) => i);
const cellKey = (c, t) => `${c}:${t}`;
const trialId = (c, t, i) => `${ROUND}-${c}-${t}-t${String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}`;
const runnerCmd = (c, t, id) => `${A.runner} --config ${c} --ticket ${t} --trial ${id} --out ${OUT}/trials/${id}.json`;
const onlySet = A.only ? new Set(A.only) : null;
const inScope = (c, t) => !onlySet || onlySet.has(cellKey(c, t));
const avg = xs => (xs.length ? xs.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0) / xs.length : null);
const median = xs => {
  if (!xs.length) return null;
  const s = [...xs].sort((a, b) => a - b);
  const m = Math.floor(s.length / 2);
  return s.length % 2 ? s[m] : (s[m - 1] + s[m]) / 2;
};
const groupBy = (xs, f) => xs.reduce((m, x) => m.set(f(x), [...(m.get(f(x)) || []), x]), new Map());
function hash(s) { let h = 2166136261; for (const ch of s) { h ^= ch.charCodeAt(0); h = Math.imul(h, 16777619); } return h >>> 0; }

let halted = null;
function halt(reason) { if (!halted) { halted = reason; log(`HALT: ${reason}`); } }

// ---------- budget ----------
const budget = { spentUsd: 0, skipped: [] };
function reserve(kind, usd, what, cap = A.spendCapUsd - A.synthReserveUsd) {
  if (budget.spentUsd + usd > cap) {
    budget.skipped.push({ kind, what, usd });
    log(`SKIP ${kind} ${what}: $${(budget.spentUsd + usd).toFixed(2)} would cross the $${cap.toFixed(2)} limit`);
    return false;
  }
  budget.spentUsd += usd;
  return true;
}

// ---------- schemas ----------
const TRIAL_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['status', 'commands_run', 'files_read'],
  properties: {
    status: { enum: ['completed', 'harness_error', 'rate_limited'] },
    error: { type: 'string' },
    commands_run: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
    files_read: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
    result: {
      type: 'object',
      properties: {
        label: { type: ['object', 'null'], properties: { category: { type: ['string', 'null'] }, priority: { type: ['string', 'null'] } } },
        reply: { type: 'string' },
        tool_calls: { type: 'integer' },
        tool_call_log: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', properties: { name: { type: 'string' }, args: { type: 'string' } } } },
        tool_errors: { type: 'integer' },
        input_tokens: { type: 'integer' },
        output_tokens: { type: 'integer' },
        runtime_ms: { type: 'integer' },
        cost_usd: { type: 'number' },
      },
    },
  },
};

const GRADE_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['ok', 'results'],
  properties: {
    ok: { type: 'boolean' },
    error: { type: 'string' },
    results: {
      type: 'array',
      items: {
        type: 'object',
        required: ['trial_id', 'category_ok', 'priority_ok'],
        properties: { trial_id: { type: 'string' }, category_ok: { type: 'boolean' }, priority_ok: { type: 'boolean' } },
      },
    },
  },
};

const JUDGE_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['scores'],
  properties: {
    scores: {
      type: 'array',
      items: {
        type: 'object',
        required: ['rid', 'tone_score', 'tone_pass', 'reason'],
        properties: { rid: { type: 'string' }, tone_score: { type: 'integer' }, tone_pass: { type: 'boolean' }, reason: { type: 'string' } },
      },
    },
  },
};

// ---------- prompts ----------
function trialPrompt(cmd, outFile) {
  return [
    'You run one trial of an evaluation. Your only job is to run one command and report its output.',
    '',
    'Run this command from the repository root, exactly as written:',
    '',
    `    ${cmd}`,
    '',
    `The command prints one JSON object and also writes it to ${outFile}. Copy its fields into "result" without changing any value.`,
    '',
    'Rules:',
    `- You may read only the command output and ${outFile}.`,
    '- Do not open, list, search, or print any other file under spe/. Do not read graders, answers, plans, or predictions.',
    '- Run the command at most twice. If it fails twice, set status to "harness_error" and put the error text in "error".',
    '- If the error mentions a rate limit or HTTP 429, set status to "rate_limited".',
    '- Put every command you ran in "commands_run" and every file you read in "files_read".',
  ].join('\n');
}

function gradePrompt(input, tag) {
  const file = `${OUT}/grade-input/${tag}.json`;
  return [
    'You run the code grader for this round. Do not judge anything yourself.',
    `1. Write this JSON array to ${file}:`,
    JSON.stringify(input),
    `2. Run: python ${GRADER} --answers ${ANSWERS} --input ${file}`,
    '3. The grader prints one JSON line per trial with trial_id, category_ok, and priority_ok. Copy them into "results" without changing any value.',
    'Set ok to false and put the error in "error" if the grader exits non-zero, prints output you cannot parse, or leaves out a trial.',
    'Do not fix the grader or the input.',
  ].join('\n');
}

function judgePrompt(ticket, replies) {
  return [
    `Read the rubric in ${JUDGE_RUBRIC} and use it to score the tone of each support reply below.`,
    `All replies answer ticket ${ticket}. You may read that ticket in ${A.ticketsPath} for context.`,
    `Do not read ${ANSWERS}, spe/predictions/, spe/plans/, or any trial file. The replies are unlabeled on purpose.`,
    'Score each reply on its own. Give tone_score as an integer from 1 to 5, tone_pass as the rubric defines it, and a one-sentence reason.',
    '',
    ...replies.map(r => `--- ${r.rid} ---\n${r.reply || '(empty reply)'}`),
  ].join('\n');
}

// ---------- leak scan ----------
// This scan checks the trial's own report of commands and reads, plus the runner's tool log.
// A grep of the saved agent transcripts after the run is a stronger check. The completeness critic asks for it.
function findLeak(t, cmd, ownFile) {
  const scrub = s => s.split(cmd).join('').split(ownFile).join('');
  const seen = [
    ...(t.commands_run || []),
    ...(t.files_read || []),
    ...((t.result && t.result.tool_call_log) || []).map(c => `${c.name} ${c.args || ''}`),
  ];
  const hit = seen.find(s => FORBIDDEN.test(scrub(s)));
  return hit || null;
}

// ---------- stages ----------
async function runTrial(config, ticket, idx, topup) {
  const id = trialId(config, ticket, idx);
  const base = { id, config, ticket, topup };
  if (halted) return { ...base, status: 'skipped', why: `halted: ${halted}` };
  if (!reserve('trial', A.est.trialAgentUsd + A.est.runnerUsd, id)) {
    halt(`spend cap reached at $${budget.spentUsd.toFixed(2)} of $${A.spendCapUsd}`);
    return { ...base, status: 'skipped', why: 'budget' };
  }
  const cmd = runnerCmd(config, ticket, id);
  const outFile = `${OUT}/trials/${id}.json`;
  let t;
  try {
    t = await agent(trialPrompt(cmd, outFile), { label: id, phase: topup ? 'Top-up' : 'Trials', schema: TRIAL_SCHEMA, model: A.model });
  } catch (e) {
    return { ...base, status: 'harness_error', error: String(e) };
  }
  const actual = t && t.result && t.result.cost_usd;
  if (typeof actual === 'number') budget.spentUsd += actual - A.est.runnerUsd;
  const peek = findLeak(t, cmd, outFile);
  if (peek) {
    halt(`answer-key leak in ${id}: ${peek}`);
    return { ...base, status: 'voided', why: peek };
  }
  return { ...base, status: t.status, error: t.error, ...(t.result || {}) };
}

async function gradeBatch(trials, tag) {
  const done = trials.filter(t => t.status === 'completed');
  if (!done.length || halted) return trials;
  if (!reserve('grade', A.est.gradeUsd, tag)) { halt('spend cap reached before grading'); return trials; }
  const input = done.map(t => ({ trial_id: t.id, ticket_id: t.ticket, label: t.label || null }));
  let g;
  try {
    g = await agent(gradePrompt(input, tag), { label: `grade ${tag}`, phase: 'Grade', schema: GRADE_SCHEMA, model: A.model });
  } catch (e) {
    halt(`grader agent failed on ${tag}: ${e}`);
    return trials;
  }
  const byId = new Map((g.results || []).map(r => [r.trial_id, r]));
  if (!g.ok || byId.size !== done.length || done.some(t => !byId.has(t.id))) {
    halt(`grader broken on ${tag}: ${g.error || 'result ids do not match input'}`);
    return trials;
  }
  return trials.map(t => {
    const r = byId.get(t.id);
    return r ? { ...t, category_ok: r.category_ok, priority_ok: r.priority_ok, pass: r.category_ok && r.priority_ok } : t;
  });
}

async function judgeBatch(trials, tag, ticket) {
  const done = trials.filter(t => t.status === 'completed');
  if (!done.length || halted) return trials;
  if (!reserve('judge', A.est.judgeUsd, tag)) { halt('spend cap reached before judging'); return trials; }
  // Blind order. The judge sees R1..Rn with no config name and no grade.
  const order = [...done].sort((a, b) => hash(tag + a.id) - hash(tag + b.id));
  const replies = order.map((t, i) => ({ rid: `R${i + 1}`, id: t.id, reply: t.reply }));
  let j;
  try {
    j = await agent(judgePrompt(ticket, replies), { label: `judge ${tag}`, phase: 'Judge', schema: JUDGE_SCHEMA, model: 'opus' });
  } catch (e) {
    halt(`judge agent failed on ${tag}: ${e}`);
    return trials;
  }
  const byRid = new Map((j.scores || []).map(s => [s.rid, s]));
  const bad = replies.find(r => {
    const s = byRid.get(r.rid);
    return !s || !Number.isInteger(s.tone_score) || s.tone_score < 1 || s.tone_score > 5;
  });
  if (bad) { halt(`judge broken on ${tag}: missing or out-of-range score for ${bad.rid}`); return trials; }
  const byId = new Map(replies.map(r => [r.id, byRid.get(r.rid)]));
  return trials.map(t => {
    const s = byId.get(t.id);
    return s ? { ...t, tone_score: s.tone_score, tone_pass: s.tone_pass, tone_reason: s.reason } : t;
  });
}

// ---------- metrics ----------
function stats(trials) {
  const count = s => trials.filter(t => t.status === s).length;
  const done = trials.filter(t => t.status === 'completed' && typeof t.pass === 'boolean');
  const judged = done.filter(t => typeof t.tone_score === 'number');
  const n = done.length;
  const num = f => done.map(f).filter(x => typeof x === 'number');
  const cells = [...groupBy(done, t => cellKey(t.config, t.ticket)).values()];
  return {
    completed_graded: n,
    harness_error: count('harness_error'),
    rate_limited: count('rate_limited'),
    voided: count('voided'),
    skipped: count('skipped'),
    category_acc: n ? done.filter(t => t.category_ok).length / n : null,
    priority_acc: n ? done.filter(t => t.priority_ok).length / n : null,
    label_acc: n ? done.filter(t => t.pass).length / n : null,
    cell_all_pass_rate: cells.length ? cells.filter(c => c.every(t => t.pass)).length / cells.length : null,
    tone_mean: avg(judged.map(t => t.tone_score)),
    tone_pass_rate: judged.length ? judged.filter(t => t.tone_pass).length / judged.length : null,
    runtime_ms_median: median(num(t => t.runtime_ms)),
    tool_calls_mean: avg(num(t => t.tool_calls)),
    tokens_mean: avg(num(t => (typeof t.input_tokens === 'number' && typeof t.output_tokens === 'number' ? t.input_tokens + t.output_tokens : null))),
    tool_errors_mean: avg(num(t => t.tool_errors)),
    cost_usd_mean: avg(num(t => t.cost_usd)),
  };
}

// ---------- Setup ----------
phase('Setup');
log(`Round ${ROUND}. Configs ${A.configs.join(', ')}. ${A.trialsPerCell} trials per cell. Spend cap $${A.spendCapUsd}.`);
log('Judge note: the tone judge is Opus. No judge from a different model family is available this round, so judge blind spots may match trial blind spots.');

let tickets = [];
if (reserve('setup', A.est.setupUsd, 'ticket ids')) {
  const setup = await agent([
    `Read ${A.ticketsPath} and return the id of every ticket, in file order.`,
    `Return ids only. Do not return ticket text, categories, or priorities. Do not open ${ANSWERS}.`,
  ].join('\n'), {
    label: 'load ticket ids',
    phase: 'Setup',
    schema: { type: 'object', required: ['ids'], properties: { ids: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } } } },
    model: A.model,
  });
  tickets = setup.ids || [];
}
if (!onlySet && tickets.length !== A.expectTickets) halt(`expected ${A.expectTickets} tickets, found ${tickets.length}`);
if (onlySet) log(`Dry run: ${[...onlySet].join(', ')}`);

// ---------- Trials, Grade, Judge ----------
phase('Trials');
const items = tickets
  .map(t => ({ ticket: t, configs: A.configs.filter(c => inScope(c, t)) }))
  .filter(it => it.configs.length);

const bundles = halted ? [] : await pipeline(
  items,
  async it => ({
    ...it,
    trials: await parallel(it.configs.flatMap(c => range(A.trialsPerCell).map(i => () => runTrial(c, it.ticket, i, false)))),
  }),
  async b => ({ ...b, trials: await gradeBatch(b.trials, b.ticket) }),
  async b => ({ ...b, trials: await judgeBatch(b.trials, b.ticket, b.ticket) }),
);
const mainTrials = bundles.flatMap(b => b.trials);

// ---------- Top-up ----------
phase('Top-up');
const graded = groupBy(mainTrials.filter(t => typeof t.pass === 'boolean'), t => cellKey(t.config, t.ticket));
const mixed = [...graded.values()]
  .filter(ts => ts.some(t => t.pass) && ts.some(t => !t.pass))
  .map(ts => ({ config: ts[0].config, ticket: ts[0].ticket }));
log(`Top-up: ${mixed.length} cells where only some trials passed. Up to ${A.topUpMax} extra trials each.`);

const topBundles = halted || !mixed.length ? [] : await pipeline(
  mixed,
  async m => ({ ...m, tag: `${m.ticket}-${m.config}-topup`, trials: await parallel(range(A.topUpMax).map(i => () => runTrial(m.config, m.ticket, A.trialsPerCell + i, true))) }),
  async b => ({ ...b, trials: await gradeBatch(b.trials, b.tag) }),
  async b => ({ ...b, trials: await judgeBatch(b.trials, b.tag, b.ticket) }),
);
const topTrials = topBundles.flatMap(b => b.trials);
const allTrials = [...mainTrials, ...topTrials];

// ---------- Synthesis ----------
phase('Synthesis');
// Headline numbers use main trials only. Top-up trials add weight to mixed cells, so they appear in a separate block.
const metrics = { main: {}, with_topup: {} };
for (const c of A.configs) {
  metrics.main[c] = stats(mainTrials.filter(t => t.config === c));
  metrics.with_topup[c] = stats(allTrials.filter(t => t.config === c));
}
const pct = x => (x == null ? 'n/a' : `${(x * 100).toFixed(1)}%`);
const fx = (x, d = 1) => (x == null ? 'n/a' : x.toFixed(d));
const headline = A.configs.map(c => {
  const m = metrics.main[c];
  return `${c}: ${pct(m.label_acc)} labels, tone ${fx(m.tone_mean, 2)}, ${fx(m.tool_calls_mean)} tool calls, $${fx(m.cost_usd_mean, 3)}/task`;
}).join(' | ');
log(`Headline: ${headline}`);

const measuredNothing = A.configs.every(c => metrics.main[c].label_acc === 1 && metrics.main[c].tone_pass_rate === 1);
if (measuredNothing) log('Every config passed everything. This round measured nothing. The next round needs harder tickets or stricter graders.');

const summary = {
  round: ROUND,
  halted,
  dry_run: !!onlySet,
  args: A,
  budget: { spent_usd_est: Number(budget.spentUsd.toFixed(2)), cap_usd: A.spendCapUsd, skipped: budget.skipped },
  headline,
  measured_nothing: measuredNothing,
  metrics,
};
const rows = allTrials.map(({ reply, tool_call_log, tone_reason, ...rest }) => rest);

let failureAnalysis = null;
let critic = null;
const synthCap = A.spendCapUsd;

if (reserve('synthesis', A.est.synthUsd, 'record results', synthCap)) {
  await agent([
    `Write these two files exactly as given. Do not change any value.`,
    `1. ${OUT}/summary.json:`,
    JSON.stringify(summary, null, 2),
    `2. ${OUT}/grades.jsonl, one JSON object per line:`,
    rows.map(r => JSON.stringify(r)).join('\n'),
  ].join('\n'), { label: 'record results', phase: 'Synthesis', model: A.model });
}

if (reserve('synthesis', A.est.synthUsd, 'failure analysis', synthCap)) {
  const failed = allTrials.filter(t => t.pass === false || t.tone_pass === false || ['harness_error', 'rate_limited', 'voided'].includes(t.status));
  failureAnalysis = await agent([
    `You analyze failures from SPE round ${ROUND}. Configs: ${A.configs.join(', ')}.`,
    `You may read ${ANSWERS}, the trial files in ${OUT}/trials/, and spe/failures.md for the failure ID format.`,
    'Group the failed trials below by cause. For each group give a suggested failure ID, a title, the configs and tickets it hits, a count, the cause, and up to 5 trial ids as evidence.',
    'Keep label failures, tone failures, and harness problems apart. A harness error or rate limit is not a model failure.',
    'Do not edit any file. The learn step writes spe/failures.md.',
    '',
    JSON.stringify(failed.map(({ reply, tool_call_log, ...rest }) => rest)),
  ].join('\n'), {
    label: 'failure analysis',
    phase: 'Synthesis',
    model: A.model,
    schema: {
      type: 'object',
      required: ['groups', 'harness_issues'],
      properties: {
        groups: {
          type: 'array',
          items: {
            type: 'object',
            required: ['failure_id', 'title', 'configs', 'count', 'cause', 'evidence'],
            properties: {
              failure_id: { type: 'string' }, title: { type: 'string' },
              configs: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } }, tickets: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
              count: { type: 'integer' }, cause: { type: 'string' }, evidence: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
            },
          },
        },
        harness_issues: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
      },
    },
  });
}

if (reserve('synthesis', A.est.synthUsd, 'completeness critic', synthCap)) {
  critic = await agent([
    `You are the completeness critic for SPE round ${ROUND}.`,
    `Read spe/predictions/${ROUND}.yaml. Compare every predicted number with the measured summary below. Use the main block for the comparison.`,
    'For each prediction give the metric, the config, the predicted value, the measured value, the stated error, whether the result is within that error, and the grader check that measured it.',
    'List any prediction that has no measured number. List any grader check the prediction names that this run did not perform.',
    'Report skipped, voided, and rate-limited trials, and say whether the halt reason (if any) makes the round unusable.',
    `Ask for a transcript grep for reads of spe/evals/ and spe/predictions/ if the run did not do one. Do not edit any file.`,
    '',
    JSON.stringify(summary),
  ].join('\n'), {
    label: 'completeness critic',
    phase: 'Synthesis',
    model: A.model,
    schema: {
      type: 'object',
      required: ['comparisons', 'unmeasured', 'gaps', 'round_usable'],
      properties: {
        comparisons: {
          type: 'array',
          items: {
            type: 'object',
            properties: {
              metric: { type: 'string' }, config: { type: 'string' },
              predicted: { type: ['number', 'null'] }, measured: { type: ['number', 'null'] },
              stated_error: { type: ['number', 'null'] }, within_error: { type: ['boolean', 'null'] },
              grader_check: { type: 'string' },
            },
          },
        },
        unmeasured: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
        gaps: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
        round_usable: { type: 'boolean' },
      },
    },
  });
}

if (halted) log(`Round halted: ${halted}. Report this before the learn step.`);
log(`Spend (estimate plus runner-reported cost): $${budget.spentUsd.toFixed(2)} of $${A.spendCapUsd}. Skipped: ${budget.skipped.length}.`);

return { ...summary, failure_analysis: failureAnalysis, critic };
```

The script would be saved as `spe/evals/harness/r04-workflow.js`. Each phase writes to these paths:
- The runner writes each trial to `spe/evals/results/r04/trials/`.
- The grader input goes to `spe/evals/results/r04/grade-input/`.
- The run records `spe/evals/results/r04/summary.json` and `spe/evals/results/r04/grades.jsonl`.

The script has not been run or dry-run yet.
